<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canggal inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/732">732</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Canggal inscription is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscription dated 732 CE, found on Mount Wukir near Magelang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>. It records the erection of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> lingam by King Sanjaya and praises his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Later kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medang-kingdom">Medang</a> kingdom traced their line to Sanjaya, and the inscription is among the earliest dated records of a Javanese kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canggal-inscription.jpg" alt="Canggal inscription" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canggal_inscription.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
